        "body": "Musashi is the player character: sharp-tongued, impatient, full of bravado, and bound to the Oni Gauntlet after being killed by Genma creatures and brought back by the gauntlet's spirit. English voice is Kenichiro Thomson; the in-game likeness is based on Toshiro Mifune, with Mifune Productions reviewing the model at multiple stages over a two-year negotiation. Musashi is not the wise older historical figure; the game uses a younger, fictional version.\n\nThe setting is early Edo-period Kyoto, roughly 1603 to 1613, decades after the Sengoku era that framed the original Onimusha trilogy. The ancient capital is being overtaken by a creeping supernatural force described variously as a dark curse, Malice, or demonic fog. Real Kyoto locations are twisted into dark-fantasy versions; Capcom consulted temple officials including Kiyomizu-dera for historical accuracy on those recreations. Combat motion capture was done with real swordsmen to keep the swordplay grounded in RE Engine physics."
